\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 1. O day of rest and gladness,
\par O day of joy and light,
\par O balm of care and sadness,
\par Most beautiful, most bright!
\par On thee the high and lowly,
\par Through ages joines in tune,
\par Sing: Holy , holy, holy,
\par To the great God Triune.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. On thee, at the creation,
\par The light first had its birth;
\par On thee, for our salvation,
\par Christ rose from depths of earth;
\par On thee, our Lord victorious
\par The Spirit sent from heaven:
\par And thus on thee most glorious
\par A triple light was given.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. To- day on weary nations
\par The heavenly manna falls;
\par To holy convocations 
\par The silver trumpet calls,
\par Where gospel light is glowing
\par With pure and radiant beams,
\par And living water flowing
\par With soul- refreshing streams.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. New graces ever gaining,
\par From this our day of rest;
\par We reach the rest remaining 
\par To spirits of the blest,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par To Holy Ghost be praises,
\par To Father, and to Son;
\par The Church her voice upraises
\par To Thee, blest Three in One.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

